   "sentenceId": 18,
   "he": "מִשֶּׁמֵּת רַבִּי בָּטְלָה עֲנָוָה וְיִרְאַת חֵטְא. אֲמַר לֵיהּ רַב יוֹסֵף לְתַנָּא: לָא תִּיתְנֵי עֲנָוָה, דְּאִיכָּא אֲנָא. אֲמַר לֵיהּ רַב נַחְמָן לְתַנָּא: לָא תִּיתְנֵי יִרְאַת חֵטְא, דְּאִיכָּא אֲנָא.",
   "en": "The final line of the mishna states that «from» the time «when Rabbi» Yehuda HaNasi «died, humility and fear of sin ceased. Rav Yosef said to the tanna» who reviewed the mishna: «Do not teach» that «humility» ceased, «for there is» still one who is humble, namely «me. Rav Naḥman» similarly «said to the tanna» who reviewed the mishna: «Do not teach» that «fear of sin» ceased, «for there is» still one who fears sin, namely «me.»"
  }
 ],
